ntdll virtual memory on the wasm memory: the base maps (docs/design/wine-unix.md,
sections 4 and 6).

- mmap, munmap, mprotect, madvise and msync in virtual.c go to the backend
  in native/wine/src/virtual_wasm.c (tw_*), which keeps its own record of the
  maps (section 6).
- The limits are 16 GiB, the memory's maximum: address_space_limit,
  user_space_limit, working_set_limit and get_host_addr_space_limit
  (section 4).
- virtual_init takes the static reserve list (tw_reserve_list, the guest
  regions) in place of the preloader's (section 4).
- Wine's bookkeeping lives in the host heap: anon_mmap_alloc and
  alloc_virtual_heap allocate there (section 4). map_view's own map at no
  fixed address goes to the backend, which takes a free range in the guest
  regions (section 6).

